{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"### Addendum — an EXISTING TEST pins the inverse, and any future fix must not break it\n\nA second independent pass confirmed the three findings above (no `run_stream`/`stream_events`/\n`isatty` commit has ever touched `src/rebar/llm/`; ADR 0089 governs; no prior ticket) and found one\ncitation I had missed that **strengthens** the not-a-bug classification rather than weakening it:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py:367` — `test_no_total_runtime_timer_mechanism`\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py:181` — `test_slow_but_alive_server_completes_under_read_timeout`\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py:256` — `test_sync_tool_is_not_interrupted_documented_caveat`\n\nThese assert that a slow-but-alive run completes and that no total-runtime timer exists — i.e. the\ntest suite **pins silence-tolerance as correct behaviour**. So the authoritative record does not\nmerely fail to require progress output; it affirmatively encodes the opposite. That is a hard\nconstraint on any future implementation: a progress heartbeat must be **purely additive emission**\nand must not introduce a total-runtime cap or otherwise truncate a healthy long run, or it will\nfail these tests and contradict ADR 0089.\n\nRejected as authority (checked, not applicable): the `silent`/`silently` language in\n`docs/llm-framework.md:336` and `docs/plan-review-gate.md:184,1101` means *semantically* silent\n(dropping a finding unrecorded), not output silence; all heartbeat/watchdog machinery in\n`docs/concurrency.md:240`, `docs/config.md:312` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/` belongs to\nthe reconciler ref-lock lease and the CI bridge canary, a different subsystem that never touches the\nLLM gate path; and `tests/unit/workflow/test_executor.py:183-192` (\"progress marker\") asserts an\nin-memory `MemoryRecorder` step status for status polling, not stderr output.\n\nCorroborating field note: open session_log `bane-coach-golly` (`003a-09ae-9983-4007`) records that\nrunning pass1 with `REBAR_LOG_LEVEL=INFO` \"made the 'hang' legible\" — independently reproducing this\ninvestigation's run-1-vs-run-3 result, and confirming that the only existing mitigation is the\nopt-in log level, not a duplicate ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787170464181223001,"uuid":"cfdfc64a-0790-47ea-9cf8-f8b7119a1b3d"}